SEL: fixed parsing of relay web pages: pages with links in their text, values on the first line of a page, the ``VER`` layout of 400-series relays, the subnet mask, full port names and invalid addresses in ``ETH`` output, settings with spaces in their values, ``SHO`` pages with a title, front panel pages without the expected heading, ``$$$$$$`` meter values, and energy metering on the SEL-351S. The ``VER`` checksum is also stored as the boot firmware checksum. A relay web login that isn't rejected, but has no session, now raises an error instead of trying more credentials.
